#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, we illustrate QPE to recover the eigenphase of a known single-qubit unitary. The unitary whose phase we want to estimate is the single-qubit phase gate applied to the target qubit:\n"
msgstr "Sa tutorial na ito, ipinakikita namin ang QPE upang mabawi ang eigenphase ng kilalang single-qubit unitary. Ang unitary na ang phase ay nais nating tantiyahin ay ang single-qubit phase gate na inilapat sa target qubit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\theta)=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[2pt]\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= e^{i\\theta\\,|1\\rangle\\!\\langle 1|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\theta)=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[2pt]\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= e^{i\\theta\\,|1\\rangle\\!\\langle 1|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We prepare its eigenstate $|\\psi\\rangle=|1\\rangle$. Because $|1\\rangle$ is an eigenvector of $U(\\theta)$ with eigenvalue $e^{i\\theta}$, the eigenphase to be estimated is:\n"
msgstr "Inihahanda namin ang eigenstate nito $|\\psi\\rangle=|1\\rangle$. Dahil ang $|1\\rangle$ ay isang eigenvector ng $U(\\theta)$ na may eigenvalue na $e^{i\\theta}$, ang eigenphase na tatantiyahin ay:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\varphi = \\frac{\\theta}{2\\pi} \\pmod{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\varphi = \\frac{\\theta}{2\\pi} \\pmod{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We set $\\theta=\\tfrac{1}{6}\\cdot 2\\pi$, so the ground-truth phase is $\\varphi=1/6$. The QPE circuit implements the controlled powers $U^{2^k}$ by applying controlled phase rotations with angles $\\theta\\cdot2^k$, then applies the inverse QFT to the counting register and measures it. The resulting bitstrings concentrate around the binary representation of $1/6$.\n"
msgstr "Itinakda namin ang $\\theta=\\tfrac{1}{6}\\cdot 2\\pi$, kaya ang ground-truth phase ay $\\varphi=1/6$. Ipinapatupad ng QPE circuit ang mga controlled power na $U^{2^k}$ sa pamamagitan ng paglalapat ng mga controlled phase rotation na may mga anggulo na $\\theta\\cdot2^k$, pagkatapos ay inilalapat ang inverse QFT sa counting register at sinusukat ito. Ang mga resultang bitstring ay nakakonsentrasyon sa paligid ng binary representation ng $1/6$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit uses $m$ counting qubits (to set the estimation precision) plus one target qubit. We begin by defining the building blocks needed to implement QPE: the Quantum Fourier Transform (QFT) and its inverse, utility functions to map between decimal and binary fractions of the eigenphase, and helpers to normalize raw counts into probabilities for comparing simulation and hardware results.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang circuit ng $m$ counting qubit (upang itakda ang estimation precision) kasama ang isang target qubit. Nagsisimula kami sa pamamagitan ng pagtukoy ng mga building block na kailangan upang ipatupad ang QPE: ang Quantum Fourier Transform (QFT) at ang inverse nito, mga utility function upang mag-map sa pagitan ng decimal at binary fraction ng eigenphase, at mga helper upang i-normalize ang mga raw count sa mga posibilidad para sa paghahambing ng simulation at hardware result.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We build the QPE circuit by preparing the counting qubits in superposition, applying controlled phase rotations to encode the target eigenphase, and finishing with an inverse QFT before measurement.\n"
msgstr "Binubuo namin ang QPE circuit sa pamamagitan ng paghahanda ng mga counting qubit sa superposition, paglalapat ng mga controlled phase rotation upang i-encode ang target eigenphase, at pagtatapos sa isang inverse QFT bago ang pagsukat.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We set the number of shots and qubits for the experiment, and encode the target phase $\\varphi = 1/6$ using $m$ binary digits. With these parameters, we build the QPE circuit that will be executed on simulation, default hardware, and Fire Opal–enhanced backends.\n"
msgstr "Itinakda namin ang bilang ng mga shot at qubit para sa eksperimento, at nag-encode ng target phase na $\\varphi = 1/6$ gamit ang $m$ binary digit. Sa mga parameter na ito, binubuo namin ang QPE circuit na isasagawa sa simulation, default hardware, at Fire Opal–enhanced backend.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run MPS simulation {#run-mps-simulation}"
msgstr "Run MPS simulation {#run-mps-simulation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we generate a reference distribution using the `matrix_product_state` simulator and convert the counts into normalized probabilities for later comparison with hardware results.\n"
msgstr "Una, bumubuo kami ng reference distribution gamit ang `matrix_product_state` simulator at kino-convert ang mga count sa normalized na mga posibilidad para sa susunod na paghahambing sa mga resulta ng hardware.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run on hardware {#run-on-hardware}"
msgstr "Run on hardware {#run-on-hardware}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run on hardware with Fire Opal {#run-on-hardware-with-fire-opal}"
msgstr "Run on hardware with Fire Opal {#run-on-hardware-with-fire-opal}"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/quantum-phase-estimation-qctrl/extracted-outputs/593334d2-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/quantum-phase-estimation-qctrl/extracted-outputs/593334d2-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simulation sets the baseline for the correct eigenphase. Default hardware runs show noise that obscures this result, as noise spreads probability across many incorrect bitstrings. With Q-CTRL Performance Management the distribution becomes sharper and the correct outcome is recovered, enabling reliable QPE at this scale.\n"
msgstr "Itinakda ng simulation ang baseline para sa tamang eigenphase. Ang mga default hardware run ay nagpapakita ng ingay na nagtatago sa resultang ito, dahil ang ingay ay kumakalat ng posibilidad sa maraming maling bitstring. Sa Q-CTRL Performance Management, ang distribusyon ay nagiging mas matalas at ang tamang kinalabasan ay nabawi, na nagbibigay-daan sa maaasahang QPE sa sukat na ito.\n"

